// A test that takes long enough to be KILLED mid-run, so the timeout path can be observed rather
// than assumed. Under the default --timeout it passes comfortably; under a --timeout below the
// sleep it is reported as TIMED OUT — which is a different outcome from DID NOT RUN, because this
// test did begin and the ones that never started did not.
//
// It lives in its own file so it is its own shard, and so a short --timeout kills only this process.

test 'takes its time'
	sleep(300)
end 'takes its time'
